messages:
maria: opened a tiny PR to add a short troubleshooting blurb: detect a service trim signal, shorten the system prompt, retry with backoff. need node + py snippets and a curl repro.

sam: paste the node snippet here and i'll lint it quickly.

maria: draft node snippet:
```javascript
const res = await fetch(RW_URL, opts);
if (res.status === 429) await retryWithBackoff();
if (res.headers.get('x-rw-context-trim')) {
  payload.system = shorten(payload.system);
  await fetch(RW_URL, opts);
}
```

kevin: i'll write the python requests version and a small pytest that mocks Response.headers.

liz: add a one-line tradeoff: use detect+shorten when you want to preserve prompt quality most of the time; proactively truncate when you need strict latency. also link to the 429/timeout errref.

docs-bot: PR #420 opened by maria  reviewers requested: @sam @kevin; labels: docs-snippet.

ci-bot: snippet-lint flagged fence lang: use "javascript" and remove trailing whitespace.

maria: fixing fences and adding a curl example that hits the test harness: `curl -i -X POST $TEST_URL -d @big_prompt.json -H "Authorization: Bearer $KEY"` expect header `x-rw-context-trim: true`. pushing fix now.

sam: will run lint and approve after green.

